xt": "The retry returned a new order, PO0002, for the full 3 docks and 3 monitors ($1,554). Before reporting, I'll check the order list for duplicates.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AJgVDZrgbi9w6YPTQZQmZ4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PO0002 is the intended order, but PO0001 is a leftover from the timed-out attempt. It duplicates the 3 docks, so I'll cancel it and get the refund.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01B62nVygs64GsAUK2p5rfhL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"order_id": "PO0001"}, "name": "cancel_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The order is placed as a single purchase order, PO0002, shipping to HQ:\n\n- **3 \u00d7 DK-200** USB-C Dock (new, not refurbished), $189 each\n- **3 \u00d7 MN-27** 27-inch 4K Monitor (new, not refurbished), $329 each\n- **Total: $1,554.** This is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval was needed.\n\nThe first attempt timed out and left a partial order, PO0001, containing only the 3 docks ($567). I cancelled PO0001 so the docks are not ordered twice, and it has been refunded. I used DK-200 rather than the DK-210 successor because DK-200 was in stock.", "type": "text"}]}]}